stateDiagram-v2
    state "Task and photo saves" as Local
    state "Pending in Room" as Pending
    state "Legacy SYNCING or FAILED row" as Legacy
    state "Request in flight (queue stays pending)" as InFlight
    state "WorkManager retry with backoff" as Backoff
    state "Waiting for sign-in" as SessionPaused
    state "Validation failure (queue retained)" as ValidationBlocked
    state "Acknowledged in Room" as Acknowledged

    [*] --> Local
    Local --> Pending: Save task and operation in one Room transaction
    Local --> Pending: Save JPEG locally, then save photo and operation in Room
    Legacy --> Pending: Restore this account's queue on worker start

    note right of Pending
        Unique work per user. App entry uses KEEP.
        Mutations append using APPEND_OR_REPLACE.
        WorkManager waits for connectivity.
    end note

    Pending --> InFlight: Active session matches owner and network is connected
    Pending --> SessionPaused: Session is absent or belongs to another account
    SessionPaused --> Pending: Sign in online as the same account
    InFlight --> SessionPaused: HTTP 401 clears only the request session
    InFlight --> Backoff: Network error, HTTP 5xx or incomplete acknowledgement
    Backoff --> Pending: Next WorkManager attempt
    InFlight --> Pending: Worker cancelled, process killed or connectivity lost
    InFlight --> ValidationBlocked: Non-retryable request rejection
    ValidationBlocked --> Pending: Correct the validation issue and trigger sync again
    InFlight --> Acknowledged: Server committed operation and client matched its acknowledgement

    note right of InFlight
        Tasks and photos follow queue sequence.
        Pending task batches finish before following photos.
        Retries carry the same stored operation ID.
        SQLite commits the mutation and account-scoped replay record together.
        Photo metadata and JPEG bytes commit in the same transaction.
    end note

    note right of Acknowledged
        Local Room status and queue removal commit together.
        Local JPEGs remain available after upload.
    end note
    Acknowledged --> [*]
